{"agent":"lane-coord","data":{"by":"grok-4.7","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":2,"detail":"A blocked-by chain is truncated at `coordinator_max_rows` without a partial-list notice, and the cut is depth-first so a direct blocker can vanish while the section looks complete. Given item X waiting on A and B, cap 2: `walk` records X then fills the cap inside A and returns before B; `partial` never gets a `\"chain\"` key, so both JSON and text omit B with no \"(N more chain not shown)\".","digest":"f9a063a5047808eb","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/services/coordinator_view.py:_chain","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/coordinator_view.py:_chain"},{"chunk":2,"detail":"The bound is not applied to every section the view returns. `owners` is built from every active ledger row before `_cut`, and `free` is the full free-name list. With `coordinator_max_rows=1`, three active lanes and twenty free lanes, `holders` is one row plus `partial[\"holders\"]`, but `owners` still has three entries and `free` has twenty. Text then prints `d[\"free\"][:10]` with no partial notice, so the cap of 1 is ignored and a longer free list is silently shortened.","digest":"bb6ef61a6c6e5145","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/services/coordinator_view.py:build","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/coordinator_view.py:build"},{"chunk":2,"detail":"One bad suite note drops the whole status read. `json.loads` of `null` or `[]` is not an `OSError`/`ValueError`, and `{**note, ...}` then raises `TypeError` outside the `suppress`. A single held slot whose note is valid JSON but not an object makes `running()` throw, so the coordinator screen fails instead of listing the other held slots.","digest":"1371fefe3ee6c6fc","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/services/suitelock.py:running","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/suitelock.py:running"},{"chunk":3,"detail":"`choices` now accepts the positional view `coordinator`, but the call only treats the boolean `--coordinator` as the coordinator screen and only then forwards `--item` as `lane`. Given `ddflow lanes coordinator --item TASK-1`, `a.get(\"view\")` is `\"coordinator\"` so the view name still reaches the API, yet `a.get(\"coordinator\")` is false, so `lane` stays `\"\"` and the blocked-by chain is omitted. The documented form `ddflow lanes --coordinator --item TASK-1` does pass the item; the newly advertised positional form does not.","digest":"fc763b86eb369bb6","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/surfaces/declared/lanes.py:34","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/surfaces/declared/lanes.py:34"}],"chunks_total":4,"coverage":"3/4 chunk(s) reviewed, 1 off-contract","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":21813,"diff_sha":"90082393b6e7008b1ef8416bf17724e8d58f93ad0492c52a27c4d12887b50607","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/CO-lanes-coordinator","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":86.5,"family":"xai","findings":4,"max_chunk_chars":8000,"model":"grok-4.7","output_digest":"ec2142c1f215a925","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/CO-lanes-coordinator.rubber_duck.grok-4.7.20261111T214734Z-3b5fdabf.jsonl","reason":"1 of 4 chunk(s) not reviewed:\n  chunk 1/4 (ddflow/api/lane_views.py, ddflow/config_sections/lanes.py): came back OFF CONTRACT: 129 chars with no STATUS: block. Not counted as reviewed.","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[2,3,4],"reviewed_head":"b5008fe6a6fdb319257e00b8d57728f00ffd366f","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/api/lane_views.py":"100644 4ddde26df66907fa824841fca045bff71f50532f","ddflow/config_sections/lanes.py":"100644 8d97a71b801996816ec6c966b55a47da9a5fc2ef","ddflow/services/coordinator_view.py":"100644 e56495ad8edccc43652a8f901ffc0a44e84588f8","ddflow/services/suitelock.py":"100644 aa4bb00d79cb27c7c0d716434479d531bd8c8e2a","ddflow/surfaces/declared/lan