{"agent":"lane-coord","data":{"by":"grok-4.7","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":3,"detail":"`running` takes an injected `now` and uses it for suite `age_s`, but the waiter count compares that same `now` to each ticket's filesystem `st_mtime`. Given `now=1_700_000_000`, `suite_queue_stale_s=60`, and a `*.ticket` whose `st_mtime` is `1_700_000_100`, `at - mtime` is `-100`, `-100 <= 60` is true, and `queued` becomes 1 even though the ticket is not a waiter observed at the supplied clock. The inverse (`now` ahead of wall mtime) drops live tickets. Any caller that freezes `now` (the parameter exists for that) gets a wrong queued count while suite ages still look coherent.","digest":"1e0e8a1f72b02b0a","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/services/suitelock.py:running","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/suitelock.py:running"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"The new assertion does not fail on the unfixed comparison, so it does not lock the bug it claims to cover. With `now=1_000.0` and a ticket just written (st_mtime near wall time, ~1.7e9), the old expression `at - st_mtime <= stale` is a large negative and still true, so `running(...)[1]` is already 1 and the test passes without the `CLOCK.wall()` change. The input that actually diverges is the other direction: `now` far ahead of wall mtime (for example `now=1_800_000_000`, live ticket mtime ≈ wall, `suite_queue_stale_s=60`) makes unfixed code drop the waiter (`queued == 0`) while the fixed line keeps it. That case is never asserted.","digest":"84e8519e1f574155","family":"xai","location":"tests/test_lanes_coordinator.py:test_the_queued_count_ignores_an_injected_now","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"LOW","title":"tests/test_lanes_coordinator.py:test_the_queued_count_ignores_an_injected_now"}],"chunks_total":1,"coverage":"1/1 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_findings":1,"delta_from":"8058adf555cd845fd7dcd0fb51f321e7fc478618","delta_raised":["84e8519e1f574155"],"delta_rounds":1,